module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.carrier_alias_refuses_its_own_carriers_constructor

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }

data carrier_alias_refuses_its_own_carriers_constructor: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "carrier_alias_refuses_its_own_carriers_constructor" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: AtCeiling { rung: StructurallyGuaranteed, ceiling_reason: "structurally guaranteed; decidable from the two declarations." as NonEmptyStr } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a value built with a carrier's own constructor is refused at a formal whose type IS that carrier. `Empty {}` / `Cons {..}` are the constructors of std.algebra FreeMonoid, std.types declares `List<element> = FreeMonoid<element>`, and operator ruling 2026-09-29 made them one type -- yet `fn take(xs: List<Int>)` refused `take(xs: Empty {})`, and a local `type ZzLT<T> = FreeMonoid<T>` refused its target's own `Empty {}`. An alias that rejects its target's constructor is below the floor whatever the realization.",
    "HARM, OBSERVED BY EXECUTION (clever-heron-784, main 6f96d86, entry compiles on srv1): 'type mismatch: expected Container(List,Primitive(element)), got Coproduct(FreeMonoid)' for A (List from std.types) and B (List from v2.std.collection), and 'expected Node(ZzLT<Primitive(T)>), got Coproduct(FreeMonoid)' for C. On main the same class refuses 35 rows under a scoped floor (quarantine_probe_disposition_witness_test, claim_cost_observation) and 7 more once gunbc#12526 widens the pool (cost_coverage acc: Empty, test_code_reference_wall).",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the fork is representational. std.algebra's FreeMonoid carrier gives its SPELLING 'List' a container_arity_row, so List<E> becomes a kernel Container, while the carrier NAME 'FreeMonoid' has no arity row and stays the declared Disj. v1.compiler.infer structured_application_site_type_mismatch_with_peeled reaches its variant-owner arm only when the formal peels to a Disj, which a Container never does. Return position looked like a counterexample but is not: declared_type_conformance_diags skips non-ground pairs, so it accepts by not judging. The element-parameter spelling (T vs element) was falsified as the discriminator by a fixture pair.",
    "A SECOND, LATENT FABRICATION FOUND IN THE SAME SEAM: application_type_expansion_head_name answers an authored LEAF after alias peeling, so a module's own `type FreeMonoid<T> { items: Int }` record was ADMITTED at a List<Int> formal on main (List peels to a leaf that also reads FreeMonoid). The repair must not trade one for the other.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent refusal of a lawful program (A/B/C) and silent admission of an unlawful one (the user FreeMonoid), both below the floor. CURRENT RUNG after gunbc PR session/clever-heron-784-carrier-constructors: structurally guaranteed at the direct-call argument seam -- a kernel container formal (List/Set/Map) is decided by DECLARATION IDENTITY (std.decl_ref DeclarationRef) of the literal's owner against the container's std.algebra carrier, before any spelling is compared; a non-kernel formal's alias is read through settled_declaration_of_type_name. Fixtures A, B, C admitted; the user FreeMonoid record and an unrelated record at List<Int> refused. CEILING: structurally guaranteed; decidable from the two declarations.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the resolver records a DeclarationRef on every type reference (the resolver-identity item), which retires the single written carrier module and the spelling-keyed container predicates enumerated in gunbc#12569; and return / let positions judge non-ground carrier pairs (split out as its own change, since it widens judgment). Set and Map carriers (FinitePowerSet, FinitelySupportedFunction) take the same identity path but declare operation records, not value constructors, so no constructor fixture exists for them.",
    "SPECIMEN, EMITTER IF-BRANCHES (XL-2 service spine, gunbc#12949, 2026-10-02): an `if` whose one branch is a value typed `List<Edge>` and whose other is a `Cons { .. }` literal was refused by the seed's Rust emission as `if branches resolve to incompatible types: Container(List,Primitive(Edge)) vs Coproduct(FreeMonoid)` -- the same alias-versus-carrier split at a join point rather than a formal. Worked around by writing the function over FreeMonoid<Edge> directly (v2.extdeps.languages.dag namespace_graft_namespace_body_members_onto), which keeps one type on both branches without a per-type helper; the class's trigger is unchanged.",
    "THE LAST SPELLING-KEYED SITE OF THE ADMISSION RUNG, REPAIRED (keen-koi-337, main 14346557686, 2026-11-01): clever-heron-784's identity gate asked the AUTHORED base name of the formal (`v1.compiler.infer is_container_type` of `authored_name_at`), so a module that declares its OWN alias of a carrier -- `type KcAlias<T> = FreeMonoid<T>`, `type KcSetAlias<T> = Set<T>` -- was answered 'this formal denotes no container' by the gate, the verdict withdrew as Absent, and the calling seam's spelling route then refused the carrier's OWN nullary constructor at that spelling: `kc_take_alias(xs: Empty {})` died with 'type mismatch: expected KcAlias, got Coproduct(Empty)'. One root, two directions (FreeMonoid and FinitePowerSet both refused, and the same refusal reached an alias of an alias), and the two canary rows beside it held -- `Empty {}` was admitted at `FreeMonoid<Int>` and an unrelated record still refused -- so the refusal was specific to the local-alias spelling, not to constructor admission.",
    "WHY THE ROSTER COULD NOT BE READ HARDER, AND WHY TWO RULES WERE MISSING RATHER THAN ONE: a module-local alias has no `std.types container_template_algebra` row, so no site of the roster read can answer for it (DESIGN section 6b -- a different rule, not the same rule at another site). And the chain walk the gate would have used, `settled_type_of_declaration` through `transparent_alias_rhs`, REFUSES an item with parameters, so a name-only settle stopped AT `type KcAlias<T> = FreeMonoid<T>` and never reached the carrier behind it. The repair is `v1.compiler.infer kernel_container_carrier_declaration`: the roster answers for the spellings it has rows for, and otherwise the authored name is followed to the declaration it aliases by `v1.compiler.infer_env settled_head_of_declaration` -- the head-only face of the chain walk, which dispatches on both alias kinds at every hop and carries no use-site arguments, the failure mode that keeps `settled_parameterized_alias` from being reused here -- and `std.types is_container_algebra_carrier` (folded from `container_template_algebra_rows`, so the alias side asks the roster's own carrier face and no second list of carrier names stands to drift). Admission still turns on declaration identity of the literal's OWNER, so the misfire side is untouched: a module's own `type FreeMonoid<T> {..}`, an unrelated record, and an alias of each all still refuse (`kc_own_freemonoid_is_not_a_list_value`, holding on main before and after, plus the two `..._refuses_an_unrelated_record` rows this change adds as its misfire controls). Witness: dag/test/claim/kernel_container_carrier_identity_witness `kc_local_alias_of_the_carrier_admits_its_constructor`, red on main, with the alias-of-alias and set-direction rows added beside it.",
    "THE Set-half OF THE NEXT-RUNG NOTE ABOVE IS SUPERSEDED: `FinitePowerSet` declares no VALUE constructor, but it is a record, so `FinitePowerSet { member: ... }` is a lawful inhabitant and a lawful argument -- `kc_local_alias_of_the_set_carrier_admits_its_constructor` is the constructor-shaped set fixture that note said did not exist. `FinitelySupportedFunction`/`Map` keep no such fixture.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "structured_kernel_container_identity_verdict"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "settled_declaration_of_type_name"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "kernel_container_carrier_declaration"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_env", decl_name: "settled_head_of_declaration"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.types", decl_name: "is_container_algebra_carrier"),
  ],
}
